<section class="section section--soft" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
  <div class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Is PicoFlow the right fit?</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading" id="fit-title">Choose PicoFlow for a conversation with clear stages.</h2>
    <div class="fit-check">
      <article class="fit-check__choice fit-check__choice--picoflow">
        <h3>Use PicoFlow for</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Customer support, booking, onboarding, guided sales, and account-service assistants.</li>
          <li>Multi-turn conversations that need durable state, validation, tools, and a reliable next step.</li>
          <li>Teams that want repeated conversation infrastructure to be shared across several assistants.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="fit-check__choice">
        <h3>Start with LangGraph when</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Your team prefers graph and state primitives as the primary authoring model.</li>
          <li>You need direct ownership of graph state, reducers, checkpointing, or execution shape.</li>
          <li>Your platform already owns the session and operations layer around the graph.</li>
          <li>You need a permissively licensed dependency.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
    <a class="evidence__link" href="/compare/langgraph/">Read the PicoFlow and LangGraph decision guide →</a>
  </div>
</section>

